LaBraM receives its input in units of 100 µV, the scale its authors tokenized, pretrained and fine-tuned it on (`/ 100` in `engine_for_vqnsp.py`, `engine_for_pretraining.py` and `engine_for_finetuning.py` of their repository): the backend divides the microvolt input by 100, for embeddings and for fine-tuning. It was fed plain microvolts before, so LaBraM embeddings and fine-tunes change and must be recomputed.
